# wrkflw datum

## Overview

**wrkflw** is a Rust CLI tool (v0.8.0) for validating and executing GitHub Actions workflows locally before pushing to GitHub. It supports Docker, Podman, emulation, and secure-emulation runtimes with a TUI interface, diff-aware filtering, expression evaluation, artifacts/cache, matrix builds, and remote triggering.

## Integration

- **CLI**: `cargo install wrkflw` (crates.io) or `brew install wrkflw`
- **Runtime**: Docker (default), Podman, emulation (no containers), secure-emulation
- **Repo**: https://github.com/bahdotsh/wrkflw
- **Workspace**: 17 crates (`wrkflw`, `wrkflw-executor`, `wrkflw-parser`, `wrkflw-validators`, `wrkflw-runtime`, `wrkflw-trigger-filter`, `wrkflw-watcher`, `wrkflw-ui`, `wrkflw-models`, `wrkflw-matrix`, `wrkflw-secrets`, `wrkflw-github`, `wrkflw-gitlab`, `wrkflw-logging`, `wrkflw-utils`, `wrkflw-evaluator`, `wrkflw-secrets`)

## Commands

```bash
wrkflw                          # Launch TUI
wrkflw validate                 # Validate all workflows
wrkflw run <workflow.yml>       # Execute workflow locally
wrkflw run --runtime emulation  # No-container mode
wrkflw run --job <job>          # Single job
wrkflw run --diff --event push  # Diff-aware execution
wrkflw watch                    # Auto-rerun on file changes
wrkflw list                     # List detected workflows
wrkflw trigger <name>           # Remote trigger via API
wrkflw validate .gitlab-ci.yml --gitlab  # GitLab support
```

## Runtime Modes

| Mode | Description | Best for |
|------|-------------|----------|
| Docker (default) | Full container isolation | Production, CI/CD |
| Podman | Rootless containers | Security-conscious |
| Emulation | No containers needed | Quick local testing |
| Secure Emulation | Sandboxed host processes | Untrusted workflows |

## Key Features

- Workflow validation with CI/CD-friendly exit codes
- Expression evaluation (`${{ ... }}` including toJSON, fromJSON, contains, startsWith)
- Container actions, JavaScript actions, composite actions (with output propagation)
- Reusable workflows (local + remote `owner/repo/path@ref`)
- Artifacts, cache, inter-job outputs (`needs.<id>.outputs.*`)
- GitHub context emulation (`GITHUB_OUTPUT`, `GITHUB_ENV`, `GITHUB_PATH`, `GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY`)
- Matrix builds (include, exclude, max-parallel, fail-fast)
- Secrets management (env, file, Vault, AWS, Azure, GCP) with masking + AES-256-GCM
- Watch mode with trigger-aware re-execution
- Interactive TUI with Workflows, Execution, DAG, Logs, Trigger, Secrets, Help tabs

## b00t Crew Roles

- **developer**: validate and test CI workflows locally before push
- **orchestrator**: evaluate CI pipeline changes across repos
- **analyst**: audit workflow correctness and coverage

## Agent Skill Coverage (Testing/CI)

Primary skill for agents that need to validate or run CI/CD workflows:
- `wrkflw validate` — structural/syntax check (pre-push gate)
- `wrkflw run --diff --event push` — simulation with change-set filtering
- `wrkflw run --runtime emulation --job <job>` — targeted job without containers

